{
  "summary": "P1 security. Ticket from Marcus Reyes (user_id 2, CFO, VIP, Finance, America/New_York, usual hours 09:00-17:00). He reports unsolicited Duo pushes early this morning and may have approved one by accident. Findings from sign-in logs: 08:10, 08:11, 08:12 UTC on 2026-10-10 are three MFA-denied Duo push attempts on VPN from hosting network IP 192.0.2.77 (Singapore), then 08:14 UTC a SUCCESSFUL VPN sign-in from the same IP via Duo push. This is consistent with MFA fatigue followed by an accidental approval. Account otherwise shows no failed password attempts. Also noted: 2026-10-09 21:30 UTC successful VPN sign-in from residential IP 198.51.100.22 in New York outside usual hours (17:30 local), which is the user's usual residential IP and needs confirming with user. Duo enrolled on Marcus's phone since 2025-12-15. Actions requested and queued for technician approval, NOT yet run: block_sign_in (approval 1), reset_password (approval 2). Still needed: approve/execute block and password reset after callback verification; kill active VPN sessions; review Singapore session activity in M365/VPN; confirm with user whether the 10-09 evening session was him; check for mailbox rules/forwarding and MFA changes; consider re-enrolling Duo if device changes. Executive target, so priority review recommended.",
  "reason": "P1 possible account compromise with a successful hosting-network sign-in after MFA fatigue, per KB-029. Always escalate. Account belongs to a VIP."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Marcus, thanks for reporting this quickly. Please do not approve any Duo push you did not start, even if it looks routine, and deny any new ones that show up. We found sign-in activity this morning from an unfamiliar overseas network that doesn't match your normal pattern, so we have requested that your sign-in and VPN access be blocked and your password be reset. Those actions need a technician's approval and have not run yet. A security engineer has been handed your ticket and will contact you by phone to verify your identity before anything is changed. Please don't reply to any email asking you to confirm your password or approve a sign-in. If you get another unexpected Duo prompt, deny it and tell us right away.",
  "internal_note": "P1 security. User is Marcus Reyes (user_id 2), CFO and VIP, Finance, NY timezone, usual hours 09:00-17:00. Logs: 2026-10-10 08:10, 08:11, 08:12 UTC show three mfa_denied Duo pushes on VPN from hosting-network IP 192.0.2.77 in Singapore. At 08:14 UTC there is a successful VPN sign-in from the same IP via duo_push, which is consistent with MFA fatigue followed by an accidental approval. No failed password attempts. Also a 2026-10-09 21:30 UTC VPN sign-in from residential IP 198.51.100.22 in New York, outside usual hours, which is this user's normal residential IP and should be confirmed with him. Duo is enrolled on his phone since 2025-12-15. Queued for technician approval, not yet run: block_sign_in (approval 1) and reset_password (approval 2). Technician must verify identity by callback to the number on file and deliver any temporary password by phone only. Escalated to Tier 2 as escalation 1. Tier 2 should review the Singapore session, revoke active sessions, check mailbox rules and forwarding, and confirm MFA settings were not changed.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-029",
    "KB-004"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
